  "description": "🪞️ Language-neutral law of `semio.hub.pair-content/v1`, the content digest two documents of one kind share when their guests answered alike. Input: a canonical checkpoint pair stream (`application/vnd.semio.canonical-checkpoint-pair.v1`: frames of a u32 big-endian length and a record; record kind 1 is the header, kind 2 a data record — part, u32 ordinal, u64 offset, u32 length, bytes —, kind 3 the terminal) and the document's id. Digest: SHA-256 of `semio.hub.pair-content/v1\\n`, then per part in ascending order `part <n> pack\\n` + the part's bytes, or, when the part starts with the SPR magic 89 53 50 52 0d 0a 1a 0a, `part <n> spr\\n` + its 32-byte header + per frame `\\nframe <kind> <flags> <rawLength or ->\\n` + its payload (only the first 32 payload bytes of a commit, kind 12); every occurrence of the document id is replaced by `<document>` in what is hashed. Left out are exactly the fields derived from the bytes before them — each frame's CRC-32C and back_len, a commit's chain hash — which differ between any two documents because they digest the id-bearing genesis record. `pairs` were captured from one B3 hub (2026-09-27): two creations of `s.note.note` and two of `2d.drawing` under the same name; `sprFrames` is each SPR part's frame list as the production decoder (`📐️format::FrameCursor`, CRC-checked) reads it; `sameContent` groups agree, `differentContent` pairs do not. Besides the ids, the two creations of one kind differ only inside those 40 SPR bytes.",
